input[type=range]{width:100%;accent-color:var(--acc)}
.opts{display:flex;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:6px 0 2px;color:var(--mute)}
.btns{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px}
button{font:inherit;padding:7px 12px;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);cursor:pointer}
button:hover{border-color:var(--acc)}
button.on{background:var(--acc);border-color:var(--acc);color:#fff}
button.primary{background:var(--acc);border-color:var(--acc);color:#fff}
.note{color:var(--mute);font-size:12.5px;margin:10px 0 0}
#status{color:var(--mute);margin-left:auto;align-self:center}
@media (max-width:520px){.row{grid-template-columns:1fr 70px}.row input{grid-column:1/-1;order:3}}
</style></head><body><main>
<h1>T2 Speakers</h1>
<p class="sub">Live controls for the "Speakers" sink. Changes apply immediately; Save writes them into 90-t2-speakers.conf.</p>

<section><h2>Crossover (LR4: two 2nd-order stages each side)</h2>
<div class="row"><label>Woofer low-pass</label><input type="range" id="lp" min="80" max="2500" step="5"><output id="lpV"></output></div>
<div class="row"><label>Tweeter high-pass</label><input type="range" id="hp" min="80" max="2500" step="5"><output id="hpV"></output></div>
<div class="opts"><label><input type="checkbox" id="link" checked> Link frequencies</label></div>
<div class="row"><label>Woofer Q</label><input type="range" id="lpQ" min="0.5" max="1.2" step="0.001"><output id="lpQV"></output></div>
<div class="row"><label>Tweeter Q</label><input type="range" id="hpQ" min="0.5" max="1.2" step="0.001"><output id="hpQV"></output></div>
<p class="note">Q 0.707 per stage = Linkwitz-Riley 4th order (flat sum at the crossover).</p>
<div class="row"><label>Woofer protection</label><input type="range" id="protect" min="30" max="150" step="1"><output id="protectV"></output></div>
<p class="note">High-pass on the woofer: removes sub-bass it can't play but would still move the cone for.</p>
</section>

<section><h2>Driver levels</h2>
<div class="row"><label>Left woofer</label><input type="range" id="woofer" min="-24" max="0" step="0.5"><output id="wooferV"></output></div>
<div class="row"><label>Left tweeter</label><input type="range" id="tweeterL" min="-24" max="0" step="0.5"><output id="tweeterLV"></output></div>
<div class="row"><label>Right tweeter</label><input type="range" id="tweeterR" min="-24" max="0" step="0.5"><output id="tweeterRV"></output></div>
<div class="opts">Invert polarity:
<label><input type="checkbox" id="wooferInv"> woofer</label>
<label><input type="checkbox" id="tweeterLInv"> L tweeter</label>
<label><input type="checkbox" id="tweeterRInv"> R tweeter</label></div>
<p class="note">Capped at 0 dB so the gain staging can never exceed full scale; a −1 dBFS limiter on each output catches filter overshoot. Use the volume for loudness.</p>
</section>

<section><h2>Bass sum into the woofer</h2>
<div class="row"><label>From left</label><input type="range" id="sumL" min="-24" max="-6" step="0.5"><output id="sumLV"></output></div>
<div class="row"><label>From right</label><input type="range" id="sumR" min="-24" max="-6" step="0.5"><output id="sumRV"></output></div>
<p class="note">Capped at −6 dB each, (L+R)/2, so a centred full-scale signal can't sum over 0 dBFS. Raise the woofer level instead.</p>
</section>

<section><h2>Test signals</h2>
<div class="btns" id="tests">
